t is allocated to a specific invoice. This ensures that there's a clear record of invoicing for this payment. The actual amount we've successfully collected from the client. This should match with the Total amount once full payment is received. Detailed status of the credit card payment, including reasons for any declines. This provides clarity on whether a transaction was successful or if there were issues. This section focuses on confirming the receipt and details of payments. It ensures the legitimacy and completeness of each transaction. The complete amount that has been successfully captured or received from the customer during the transaction. This unique code, assigned by the banking institution, serves as a specific reference for the transaction. It's crucial for tracking and auditing purposes. Upload the insurer's official receipt here. This document provides evidence of the transaction and is vital for record-keeping and any future verifications. The receipt number provided by the insurer upon successful completion of the transaction. Incorrect payment information, proof of payment or receipt provided Payment proof or receipt is not readable Insufficient documentation No proof of discount approval No proof of Credit approval Other reasons Select the checkbox to enable the 'Confirm' button and proceed This lead is now locked as the policy has been booked. If changes are needed, please make them through the 'Send Update' section via 'Correction of Policy' Click to initiate AML screening and complete the KYC process. Selection is disabled due to Credit Approval applied. Please remove Credit Approval to modify This field is now locked because the payment has been successfully captured. If any changes are required, please proceed by booking the policy, then go to 'Send Update', select 'Add Update', and choose 'Correction of Policy'. You cannot proceed with transaction approval until the Insurer AML status is cleared. You cannot proceed with transaction approval