sparency. CHQ Cheque null The customer pays using a cheque that has the current date on it. Ensure the cheque details are correctly filled out and verify its authenticity. CR Credit null null CA Credit Approval null This indicates a special payment arrangement where there isn't an immediate payment. Instead, the advisor seeks permission from higher-ups to issue the policy first, often due to specific circumstances or arrangements. CC Credit Card null The customer settles their payment using a credit card. This can be done in-person or electronically. Ensure to get authorization and proper documentation for such transactions. IN_PL Insure Now, Pay Later null This flexible payment option allows the customer to obtain their insurance policy first and then set up an instalment-based payment plan to settle the total amount due. IP Insurer Payment null This indicates a direct payment to the insurance provider. It's not a payment to the broker or agency but directly to the company underwriting the insurance. IPL Insurer Payment Link null Enter the payment link received from the insurer. This insurer payment link will be included in the email to the customer to complete the payment for their health insurance policy MP Multiple Payment null When the customer opts to use various methods or sources to pay the total amount, this option is chosen. It's often used in conjunction with the split payment method. PP Partial Payment null This payment method is used when the total amount is divided into multiple payments over a set period. It's typically chosen for semi-annual, quarterly, or monthly payment frequencies. PDC Post Dated Cheque null This is a cheque given by the customer with a future date on it. It's a commitment to pay and cannot be cashed until the date mentioned. PPR Proforma Payment Request null This is a preliminary payment request drafted and shared with the customer for their review or action. Such requests typically need approval from senior management before bei